244
00:09:53,551 --> 00:09:54,385
[Audrey, in English] Hurry, hurry.

245
00:09:54,468 --> 00:09:57,930
[indistinct]

246
00:10:01,434 --> 00:10:02,935
Tape Measure, Tape Measure.

247
00:10:03,019 --> 00:10:04,604
Help Mama Mary and Adopted Thread.

248
00:10:04,687 --> 00:10:06,063
They're being chased!

249
00:10:06,147 --> 00:10:07,440
Go to them. Move now!

250
00:10:07,523 --> 00:10:09,609
What? Wait, hold on.

251
00:10:10,484 --> 00:10:12,403
I thought it was just a date.

252
00:10:12,486 --> 00:10:13,821
Why do they want to kidnap them?

253
00:10:13,904 --> 00:10:14,822
What happened?

254
00:10:14,905 --> 00:10:16,365
I don't know. I don't know.

255
00:10:16,449 --> 00:10:18,284
My muscle already hurts.

256
00:10:18,367 --> 00:10:20,036
Just go to them!

257
00:10:20,745 --> 00:10:22,705
I can't follow. I can't move.

258
00:10:22,788 --> 00:10:24,290
[groans]

259
00:10:24,373 --> 00:10:26,208
Okay. All right, all right. Roger.

260
00:10:26,292 --> 00:10:27,752
[music swells]

261
00:10:27,835 --> 00:10:29,962
Hey. Thread 3, Thread 3!

262
00:10:30,046 --> 00:10:31,339
[in English] Do you copy?

263
00:10:31,422 --> 00:10:37,345
Tailor AFAM is chasing
Mama Mary and Adopted Thread!

264
00:10:37,428 --> 00:10:38,679
Follow them, Thread 3!

265
00:10:38,763 --> 00:10:39,722
[in English] Do you copy?!

266
00:10:39,805 --> 00:10:40,848
Thread 3!

267
00:10:40,931 --> 00:10:42,058
[music fades]

268
00:10:42,141 --> 00:10:44,810
Hello? Hello, Thread 1?

269
00:10:44,894 --> 00:10:46,270
[in English] Do you read me?

270
00:10:46,354 --> 00:10:50,191
We're already in position,
with Mini Thread.

271
00:10:50,274 --> 00:10:52,818
[in English] Hello? Any instructions?

272
00:10:52,902 --> 00:10:54,820
Hello, Thread 1? [clicks tongue]

273
00:10:54,904 --> 00:10:57,323
[sighs] We're so bored here.

274
00:10:57,907 --> 00:10:59,700
Feels like we're not doing anything.

275
00:10:59,784 --> 00:11:02,286
We've already eaten so many banana cues!

276
00:11:03,496 --> 00:11:04,330
[sighs]

277
00:11:04,413 --> 00:11:06,290
Hello? Hello, Thread-- [clicks tongue]

278
00:11:06,374 --> 00:11:08,000
[in English] I can't reach anyone, Ame.

279
00:11:08,084 --> 00:11:09,085
[grunts]

280
00:11:09,752 --> 00:11:10,961
[sighs]

281
00:11:11,045 --> 00:11:12,630
[Kurt] We're blind here.

282
00:11:14,382 --> 00:11:15,424
- [device blips]
- Uh.

283
00:11:17,593 --> 00:11:19,970
Uh. [laughs]

284
00:11:20,054 --> 00:11:21,263
Low battery.

285
00:11:21,347 --> 00:11:22,264
[laughs]

286
00:11:22,348 --> 00:11:23,641
That's why they can't hear me.

287
00:11:23,724 --> 00:11:25,684
- [laughs]
- That's why.

288
00:11:26,268 --> 00:11:29,146
Eh, maybe the mission is done.

289
00:11:29,230 --> 00:11:31,690
- Mm-hmm.
- Maybe the operation is okay.

290
00:11:31,774 --> 00:11:33,025
Should we go home?

291
00:11:33,109 --> 00:11:34,693
[Kurt] Oh, wish we all could.

292
00:11:34,777 --> 00:11:35,611
Oh.

293
00:11:35,694 --> 00:11:37,613
[rousing music playing]

294
00:11:37,696 --> 00:11:39,281
[tense music playing]

295
00:11:39,365 --> 00:11:40,366
Uh. That's them, right?

296
00:11:41,117 --> 00:11:42,910
[Kurt, in English] Wow! They're dedicated.

297
00:11:44,328 --> 00:11:46,914
Why are they running so fast?

298
00:11:46,997 --> 00:11:48,416
I thought it was just jogging?

299
00:11:48,499 --> 00:11:50,793
- Oh, wait.
- Why does it look like they're chasing--

300
00:11:50,876 --> 00:11:52,128
Yes.

301
00:11:52,211 --> 00:11:53,379
Uh, I think I know that guy.

302
00:11:56,590 --> 00:11:57,758
Uh, that's him!

303
00:11:57,842 --> 00:12:00,219
The-- The ambassador's bodyguard. That's…

304
00:12:00,302 --> 00:12:01,387
Samir!

305
00:12:01,470 --> 00:12:02,805
That's Samir!

306
00:12:02,888 --> 00:12:05,349
[in English] He's chasing Mama Mary
and Adopted Thread!

307
00:12:05,850 --> 00:12:07,143
- Uh--
- Oh.

308
00:12:07,643 --> 00:12:08,686
You're clueless.

309
00:12:09,437 --> 00:12:10,479
Are you still clueless?

310
00:12:10,563 --> 00:12:11,981
Is that Audrey?!

311
00:12:12,773 --> 00:12:14,024
- Wait, wait, wait. Auntie, Auntie.
- [panting]

312
00:12:14,108 --> 00:12:15,985
We need to get off the track,
so they won't follow us.

313
00:12:16,068 --> 00:12:17,236
[in English] Okay, yes. Let's go!

314
00:12:18,654 --> 00:12:20,030
That's them, boss.

315
00:12:20,114 --> 00:12:21,574
Wow.

316
00:12:21,657 --> 00:12:23,534
They still managed to stroll around.

317
00:12:24,201 --> 00:12:25,786
Let's go. We need to get them.

318
00:12:26,871 --> 00:12:28,497
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!

319
00:12:29,123 --> 00:12:30,124
Your payment!

320
00:12:32,835 --> 00:12:33,794
[in English] Here, here, here.

321
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:36,130
- [thuds]
- [groans]

322
00:12:36,213 --> 00:12:37,339
[Gavin] Auntie!

323
00:12:37,423 --> 00:12:39,049
[groans]

324
00:12:39,133 --> 00:12:40,384
Auntie, sorry, but you need to get up.

325
00:12:40,468 --> 00:12:41,677
They might catch us.

326
00:12:41,760 --> 00:12:42,928
[foreboding music playing]

327
00:12:43,012 --> 00:12:44,346
[in English] Come on.

328
00:12:44,430 --> 00:12:45,473
Auntie, let's go.

329
00:12:45,556 --> 00:12:46,849
[Gavin, in English] I got you, I got you.

330
00:12:47,558 --> 00:12:49,018
- Let's go.
- [gasps]

331
00:12:50,811 --> 00:12:52,104
- [in English] Here.
- [in English] Okay.

332
00:12:54,190 --> 00:12:55,858
- [Gavin] Here, here.
- [whimpering]

333
00:12:58,611 --> 00:12:59,445
- [grunts]
- [gasps]

334
00:13:00,446 --> 00:13:01,322
[groans]

335
00:13:04,158 --> 00:13:06,410
[Samir, in English] Where do you think

336
00:13:07,286 --> 00:13:09,205
you are going?

337
00:13:09,288 --> 00:13:12,041
[in English] Both of you
come with me. Right now!

338
00:13:12,124 --> 00:13:15,169
[tense music playing]

339
00:13:18,255 --> 00:13:21,717
[in English] You think that you
can protect her from me?!

340
00:13:22,676 --> 00:13:24,595
[in English] You want to be a hero.

341
00:13:24,678 --> 00:13:25,763
[ominous music playing]

342
00:13:25,846 --> 00:13:28,891
[in English] Who else
wants to be a hero? Anyone?!

343
00:13:31,352 --> 00:13:32,520
[gun cocks]

344
00:13:32,603 --> 00:13:34,104
Go to hell!

345
00:13:34,188 --> 00:13:37,274
[in English] Nobody leaves. All of you!

346
00:13:38,108 --> 00:13:40,819
[in English] Drop your gun,
or there will be blood.

347
00:13:42,238 --> 00:13:44,365
Who are you trying to scare, huh?

348
00:13:44,949 --> 00:13:46,825
Hey, Blondie! Your payment!

349
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:49,370
You think you can escape from me?!

350
00:13:49,453 --> 00:13:51,080
Later, Fatty!

351
00:13:51,163 --> 00:13:52,957
You know I'm busy here, right?!

352
00:13:53,457 --> 00:13:55,292
[grunting]

353
00:13:55,376 --> 00:13:58,462
[action music playing]

354
00:14:03,592 --> 00:14:05,844
Where are they?

355
00:14:05,928 --> 00:14:08,556
They passed here, but they ran fast.

356
00:14:09,431 --> 00:14:12,184
Actually, Ame, stay here.

357
00:14:12,268 --> 00:14:13,519
[in English] I'll go look for them.

358
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:20,442
Hey, bro!

359
00:14:21,110 --> 00:14:22,820
There's a royal rumble there.

360
00:14:23,445 --> 00:14:25,698
AFAM versus blond thug

361
00:14:25,781 --> 00:14:27,658
versus fat vendor with a bolo!

362
00:14:27,741 --> 00:14:29,285
Huh? Where?

363
00:14:29,368 --> 00:14:30,828
[Kurt] Hey, guys!

364
00:14:30,911 --> 00:14:31,996
How are you?

365
00:14:32,621 --> 00:14:33,581
Question.

366
00:14:34,456 --> 00:14:37,793
In that rumble,
was there a sexy woman there?

367
00:14:37,877 --> 00:14:39,920
[in English] Do you recall seeing one?

368
00:14:40,004 --> 00:14:41,338
Yes!

369
00:14:41,422 --> 00:14:43,340
She looked like Mama Mary.

370
00:14:43,424 --> 00:14:45,968
And she was with a handsome young man.

371
00:14:46,051 --> 00:14:48,804
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

372
00:14:49,388 --> 00:14:50,639
Wait, uh--

373
00:14:51,891 --> 00:14:53,684
[grunting and groaning]

374
00:14:55,019 --> 00:14:57,813
[Audrey screams] Gavin! Gavin!

375
00:14:57,897 --> 00:14:59,148
[in English] Be careful!

376
00:14:59,231 --> 00:15:00,733
[grunts and groans]

377
00:15:00,816 --> 00:15:02,985
Gavin! Gavin!

378
00:15:03,068 --> 00:15:05,446
[in English] Let him go! Gavin!

379
00:15:08,532 --> 00:15:10,367
[grunts]

380
00:15:18,459 --> 00:15:20,544
[grunting and groaning]

381
00:15:38,562 --> 00:15:40,689
[in English] Guys, let's go.

382
00:15:40,773 --> 00:15:43,442
[Kurt] Mama Mary!
Children of the thread, let's go!

383
00:15:44,276 --> 00:15:45,819
- Come on, come on.
- [in English] Let's go!

384
00:15:45,903 --> 00:15:48,155
[grunting and groaning]

385
00:15:54,203 --> 00:15:55,913
[in English] Sir, they're gone!

386
00:15:55,996 --> 00:15:56,997
[music fades]

387
00:15:57,081 --> 00:15:58,749
- [in English] They're gone.
- [in English] Let's go! Let's go.

388
00:16:01,251 --> 00:16:03,504
Hey! Come back here! We're not done!

389
00:16:03,587 --> 00:16:05,172
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey! Your payment!

390
00:16:05,255 --> 00:16:06,799
[grunts]

391
00:16:07,383 --> 00:16:09,843
[in English] Oh! Keep the change!

392
00:16:10,511 --> 00:16:11,845
Move your ass!

393
00:16:11,929 --> 00:16:13,764
[rousing music playing]

394
00:16:13,847 --> 00:16:16,266
I don't know what to do with you anymore!

395
00:16:16,892 --> 00:16:18,894
[Cita] Good thing no one got hurt!

396
00:16:19,770 --> 00:16:22,147
Instead of just thinking about Atoy,

397
00:16:22,231 --> 00:16:23,565
you made things worse!

398
00:16:24,274 --> 00:16:26,694
Sorry, Miss Cita.

399
00:16:26,777 --> 00:16:28,195
My God!

400
00:16:28,278 --> 00:16:32,324
That was the only way
we thought we could help Atoy.

401
00:16:32,408 --> 00:16:34,535
We didn't know

402
00:16:34,618 --> 00:16:36,203
that would happen.

403
00:16:36,286 --> 00:16:38,038
[Ame] It was Emerson.

404
00:16:38,122 --> 00:16:40,708
You're the one
who planned everything, right?

405
00:16:40,791 --> 00:16:42,793
Oh, come on, Ame.

406
00:16:43,711 --> 00:16:44,962
Stop with the blaming!

407
00:16:45,713 --> 00:16:49,216
We all just wanted to save Atoy.

408
00:16:49,967 --> 00:16:52,344
I spoke to Atoy in my dream.

409
00:16:53,804 --> 00:16:55,139
[in English] I had the purpose, you know?

410
00:16:55,222 --> 00:16:56,974
So much happened.

411
00:16:57,057 --> 00:16:59,476
We didn't expect Samir to chase us.

412
00:16:59,560 --> 00:17:01,937
And then, Daddy's men were also there.

413
00:17:02,021 --> 00:17:04,106
So, two groups were chasing us.

414
00:17:04,189 --> 00:17:06,358
My God. Good thing you escaped!

415
00:17:06,442 --> 00:17:09,194
But you shouldn't have brought Audrey!

416
00:17:09,278 --> 00:17:11,530
She has a child waiting for her!

417
00:17:11,613 --> 00:17:14,033
What if she got hurt?!
What about the child?!

418
00:17:16,326 --> 00:17:18,037
Where is Audrey?

419
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:19,747
She's in the room, Mom.

420
00:17:19,830 --> 00:17:21,415
She's resting, with Janine.

421
00:17:21,498 --> 00:17:25,377
But guys, it wasn't for nothing.

422
00:17:26,295 --> 00:17:29,673
Because I overheard Samir
and his companion.

423
00:17:29,757 --> 00:17:32,593
Their plan is to kidnap Mama Mary.

424
00:17:32,676 --> 00:17:34,386
Oh, Audrey.

425
00:17:35,429 --> 00:17:37,848
So, they want to kidnap her
to blackmail Atoy.

426
00:17:37,931 --> 00:17:40,642
So, what does that mean? They have Atoy.

427
00:17:41,185 --> 00:17:42,936
- [Emerson] Oh.
- So, how would we know

428
00:17:43,020 --> 00:17:44,813
where Brother Atoy is now?

429
00:17:45,856 --> 00:17:47,649
What if we kidnap Samir?

430
00:17:48,317 --> 00:17:49,526
- What?!
- Why?

431
00:17:49,610 --> 00:17:51,028
Is he the only one who can kidnap?

432
00:17:51,111 --> 00:17:52,404
We can too.

433
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:54,364
Look.

434
00:17:54,448 --> 00:17:57,159
If we kidnap Samir,

435
00:17:57,743 --> 00:17:59,495
we'll interrogate him.

436
00:17:59,578 --> 00:18:03,791
We'll put him under that swinging light.

437
00:18:03,874 --> 00:18:04,833
Like that.

438
00:18:06,418 --> 00:18:08,170
We'll make him confess

439
00:18:08,253 --> 00:18:09,671
where he brought Atoy.

440
00:18:09,755 --> 00:18:11,548
[in English] What do you think?

441
00:18:11,632 --> 00:18:13,258
But how will we do that?

442
00:18:13,342 --> 00:18:16,345
We don't even know
where on earth that man is.

443
00:18:16,428 --> 00:18:17,805
[action music playing]

444
00:18:17,888 --> 00:18:20,557
[in English] Of all the places--
Maybe the,

445
00:18:20,641 --> 00:18:21,725
the…

446
00:18:21,809 --> 00:18:24,561
- the Chocolate Beach in Bohol and the…
- [in English] Chocolate Beach.

447
00:18:24,645 --> 00:18:26,313
the Boracay Hills.

448
00:18:26,396 --> 00:18:27,981
- [in English] Okay.
- [stammers, in English] It's-- But it's…

449
00:18:28,065 --> 00:18:28,899
[in English] It's far.

450
00:18:28,982 --> 00:18:31,276
[in English] If you want
to-to-to be nearby,

451
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:33,403
it's all-- Of all of the places, it's, uh…

452
00:18:33,487 --> 00:18:36,698
Las, uh, Filipinas in Quezon City.

453
00:18:36,782 --> 00:18:38,742
[in English] Yes. Very beautiful.
It's my favorite.

454
00:18:38,826 --> 00:18:40,828
Uh, very, uh…

455
00:18:40,911 --> 00:18:41,787
relaxing!

456
00:18:41,870 --> 00:18:43,247
Especially, uh…

457
00:18:43,330 --> 00:18:46,667
[in English] Casa Monroy. The…
Of all of the places.

458
00:18:47,292 --> 00:18:48,377
Hmm.

459
00:18:48,961 --> 00:18:50,212
I'll handle it.

460
00:18:50,921 --> 00:18:53,048
I know his schedule tomorrow.

461
00:18:53,674 --> 00:18:57,427
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

462
00:19:00,806 --> 00:19:01,890
Enough.

463
00:19:03,267 --> 00:19:05,519
Don't continue with your plans,

464
00:19:06,103 --> 00:19:10,482
and you can't be involved in any mission

465
00:19:10,566 --> 00:19:12,985
if you can't carry it out!

466
00:19:14,862 --> 00:19:15,863
I'll do it.

467
00:19:16,446 --> 00:19:18,365
I'll be the one to save Agent Padua.

468
00:19:18,448 --> 00:19:20,784
Wait a minute, Uno!

469
00:19:20,868 --> 00:19:24,037
You're not the only one
capable of finding a way.

470
00:19:24,705 --> 00:19:27,708
Even if Miss Siony's fence
is taller than me,

471
00:19:27,791 --> 00:19:29,835
I can still help.

472
00:19:30,669 --> 00:19:31,837
[Cita] Wait, wait.

473
00:19:32,337 --> 00:19:33,338
That's right!

474
00:19:33,422 --> 00:19:35,465
Let's leave it to Uno.

475
00:19:35,549 --> 00:19:37,676
He's more trained for missions like this!

476
00:19:38,677 --> 00:19:41,305
What chance do we have
against Atoy's enemies?!

477
00:19:41,388 --> 00:19:44,683
Mom, I can't just wait
for Brother Atoy to be saved.

478
00:19:45,225 --> 00:19:47,561
I feel useless here.

479
00:19:48,604 --> 00:19:49,813
And Uno,

480
00:19:50,856 --> 00:19:53,650
you can't take deprive us
the chance to act too.

481
00:19:54,526 --> 00:19:57,196
We love Brother Atoy,
so, we'll fight as well.

482
00:19:58,071 --> 00:20:00,699
We had miscommunication earlier.
It's true.

483
00:20:00,782 --> 00:20:03,285
And our coordination was weak.

484
00:20:03,368 --> 00:20:04,661
[in English] But we can do better.

485
00:20:05,537 --> 00:20:08,707
[in English] I think, with
a little planning and a little strategy,

486
00:20:08,790 --> 00:20:10,125
we can still save Atoy.

487
00:20:10,209 --> 00:20:12,085
[in English] And I believe
in what we're doing, so…

488
00:20:12,169 --> 00:20:13,503
I'm still joining.

489
00:20:13,587 --> 00:20:16,673
And just because you're good at combat

490
00:20:16,757 --> 00:20:19,218
doesn't mean you alone decide
who helps and who doesn't.

491
00:20:19,301 --> 00:20:21,011
This isn't the time to show off.

492
00:20:21,094 --> 00:20:22,721
I'm not showing off.

493
00:20:22,804 --> 00:20:25,307
[somber music playing]

494
00:20:25,390 --> 00:20:26,892
All I mean, Gavin,

495
00:20:28,060 --> 00:20:31,772
is I don't want anyone to get hurt!

496
00:20:32,356 --> 00:20:34,107
We failed earlier.

497
00:20:34,191 --> 00:20:36,151
And Miss Cita is worried!

498
00:20:36,235 --> 00:20:37,277
Right?

499
00:20:37,361 --> 00:20:40,155
Our enemies earlier…

500
00:20:40,239 --> 00:20:42,241
We struggled to escape from them!

501
00:20:42,866 --> 00:20:46,620
This isn't a joke!

502
00:20:47,579 --> 00:20:49,289
So, let me do it.

503
00:20:49,373 --> 00:20:52,334
Leave it to me. I can handle it.

504
00:20:52,417 --> 00:20:53,752
[Emerson clears throat]

505
00:20:54,419 --> 00:20:56,922
You know, Uno…

506
00:20:58,298 --> 00:21:00,050
it's not just courage that's needed.

507
00:21:00,634 --> 00:21:02,302
There must also be teamwork.

508
00:21:04,096 --> 00:21:08,809
It's like thread, right?

509
00:21:09,977 --> 00:21:12,145
If it's just one strand…

510
00:21:14,064 --> 00:21:16,316
it's easy to break.

511
00:21:17,109 --> 00:21:20,070
But if one strand

512
00:21:21,196 --> 00:21:24,408
is added with another and another

513
00:21:24,992 --> 00:21:29,204
and another and another and another… Mmm.

514
00:21:29,288 --> 00:21:30,163
Right?

515
00:21:30,247 --> 00:21:32,624
It becomes a bundle.

516
00:21:32,708 --> 00:21:35,335
[pensive music playing]

517
00:21:35,419 --> 00:21:37,170
It can't be broken anymore

518
00:21:37,796 --> 00:21:40,299
because it's stronger and tougher.

519
00:21:41,174 --> 00:21:43,552
That's how we should be in our mission.

520
00:21:44,136 --> 00:21:45,804
We must be together.

521
00:21:49,474 --> 00:21:50,851
I already know

522
00:21:50,934 --> 00:21:54,271
where we can find Samir tomorrow night.

523
00:21:55,647 --> 00:21:57,774
He'll be with innocent people,

524
00:21:57,858 --> 00:22:00,235
so we can't just kidnap him there.

525
00:22:01,278 --> 00:22:02,988
We need to be in disguise,

526
00:22:03,655 --> 00:22:06,533
so we can smoothly take him
without anyone else harmed.

527
00:22:07,784 --> 00:22:10,620
Oh, I'm joining that.

528
00:22:11,121 --> 00:22:13,290
I don't want to wait alone again.

529
00:22:13,874 --> 00:22:16,918
- Karla.
- [Karla] I don't want to wait alone.

530
00:22:18,170 --> 00:22:20,047
We're complete now,
the children of the thread.

531
00:22:20,630 --> 00:22:22,174
So, shall we?

532
00:22:22,674 --> 00:22:24,468
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

533
00:22:24,551 --> 00:22:26,053
Let's save Atoy!

534
00:22:26,136 --> 00:22:27,095
[in English] Okay!

535
00:22:27,804 --> 00:22:29,347
- [in English] Yes! Let's do this, guys!
- [in English] Let's go!

536
00:22:29,431 --> 00:22:31,892
[in English] We do it right this time.
For Atoy.

537
00:22:31,975 --> 00:22:33,226
- [in English] Okay!
- [Karla] That's it!

538
00:22:33,310 --> 00:22:35,771
[in English] Let's go! Let's do this!

539
00:22:35,854 --> 00:22:40,108
[in English] OKA. Operation Kidnap AFAM.

540
00:22:40,192 --> 00:22:41,276
[in English] Let's go! Let's go!

541
00:22:41,359 --> 00:22:43,070
Let's go, children of the thread!

542
00:22:43,153 --> 00:22:44,154
Children of the thread!

543
00:22:44,237 --> 00:22:45,322
- Fight! Let's go!
- [Karla, in English] Let's go.

544
00:22:45,405 --> 00:22:47,949
[in English] So,
this is what we're gonna do.

545
00:22:48,033 --> 00:22:51,328
[in English] Listen to me, listen to me,
listen to me. Okay.

546
00:22:51,995 --> 00:22:53,163
Listen.

547
00:22:53,246 --> 00:22:55,874
[groans]

548
00:22:55,957 --> 00:22:57,209
[pensive music playing]

549
00:22:57,292 --> 00:22:59,628
I'll teach you how to open it.

550
00:22:59,711 --> 00:23:01,213
[Atoy] This will be quick.

551
00:23:01,880 --> 00:23:04,800
So, insert what I gave you.

552
00:23:05,634 --> 00:23:07,260
Then put it into the hole.

553
00:23:10,722 --> 00:23:12,432
About halfway only.

554
00:23:12,974 --> 00:23:16,144
Then turn it

555
00:23:16,228 --> 00:23:18,688
about 30 degrees to the right.

556
00:23:20,232 --> 00:23:21,566
[in English] What are you talking about?

557
00:23:23,860 --> 00:23:26,488
[in English] Oh, we…

558
00:23:26,571 --> 00:23:28,782
[in English] We miss our family.

559
00:23:28,865 --> 00:23:31,993
[in English] Yes. We talk about love.

560
00:23:37,457 --> 00:23:38,959
[Atoy] Then, Lily,

561
00:23:39,042 --> 00:23:41,294
there's a button on the left.

562
00:23:42,254 --> 00:23:43,755
Once you've turned it…

563
00:23:44,589 --> 00:23:45,590
[Atoy sighs]

564
00:23:45,674 --> 00:23:47,676
…match it with the click.

565
00:23:49,177 --> 00:23:51,388
Then you'll hear…

566
00:23:51,471 --> 00:23:53,431
- [sighs]
- [clicks]

567
00:23:53,515 --> 00:23:55,475
There. I removed it.

568
00:23:56,560 --> 00:23:57,686
I removed it.

569
00:23:57,769 --> 00:23:59,062
- [suspicious music playing]
- [gate rattles]

570
00:24:01,064 --> 00:24:01,940
[Atoy groans]

571
00:24:04,234 --> 00:24:05,861
[henchman 2] You two, eat now.

572
00:24:05,944 --> 00:24:07,612
You'll surely like this.

573
00:24:08,488 --> 00:24:09,823
[Lily] I'll eat later.

574
00:24:09,906 --> 00:24:11,950
I'll save that for later.

575
00:24:15,745 --> 00:24:16,663
[henchman 2, in English] Is he dead?

576
00:24:17,455 --> 00:24:20,417
[henchman 1, in English]
No. Very weak and stinky.

577
00:24:29,050 --> 00:24:30,427
[doo slams shut]

578
00:24:31,136 --> 00:24:31,970
[music fades]

579
00:24:32,053 --> 00:24:35,223
Atoy, Atoy, they're gone.

580
00:24:36,224 --> 00:24:38,602
[tense music playing]

581
00:24:43,565 --> 00:24:44,608
All right.

582
00:24:45,108 --> 00:24:46,651
[Lily] You should eat, Atoy.

583
00:24:47,485 --> 00:24:49,362
You haven't eaten yet.

584
00:24:50,363 --> 00:24:52,032
I'm fine. Don't mind me.

585
00:24:54,701 --> 00:24:55,994
After you eat,

586
00:24:56,995 --> 00:24:59,748
don't throw away the bone.
We can still use it.

587
00:24:59,831 --> 00:25:04,127
Okay, but… I can't be the only one eating.

588
00:25:04,211 --> 00:25:05,795
You should eat too. You need strength.

589
00:25:08,965 --> 00:25:10,759
[speaks softly] Okay.

590
00:25:11,301 --> 00:25:16,056
[music swells]

591
00:25:39,329 --> 00:25:40,163
[music fades]

592
00:25:40,247 --> 00:25:44,793
[electronic blipping]

593
00:25:45,877 --> 00:25:48,713
[intense music playing]

594
00:25:49,339 --> 00:25:50,257
- [grunts]
- [henchman 1, in English] You eat!

595
00:25:50,340 --> 00:25:51,967
[Lily mumbles]

596
00:25:52,050 --> 00:25:53,009
[bone swishes]

597
00:25:53,093 --> 00:25:54,344
‪UP NEXT

598
00:25:54,427 --> 00:25:55,720
- [bone swishes]
- [grunts]

599
00:25:56,554 --> 00:25:59,599
So, how's it going? Have you found
the location of Tailor AFAM?

600
00:25:59,683 --> 00:26:01,476
[Emerson] <i>Update me</i>
<i>once you've found him, okay.</i>

601
00:26:01,559 --> 00:26:03,019
- [in English] Copy.
- [in English] Okay.

602
00:26:03,103 --> 00:26:04,104
[in English] Roger that.

603
00:26:04,187 --> 00:26:05,063
[in English] Yes, ma'am!

604
00:26:05,146 --> 00:26:08,108
[in English] Okay. One, two, three, smile.

605
00:26:08,191 --> 00:26:09,734
[in English] You're so cute.

606
00:26:09,818 --> 00:26:12,237
[Kurt, in English] Thank you
so much. Oh! Sorry!

607
00:26:12,320 --> 00:26:14,239
[in English] You look familiar.

608
00:26:15,407 --> 00:26:16,741
[henchman 2] Is this
what you're looking for?

609
00:26:17,993 --> 00:26:20,078
Raise your hands, or I'll shoot you!

610
00:26:20,161 --> 00:26:22,414
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

611
00:26:23,581 --> 00:26:25,417
- [grunts & gunshot]
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

612
00:26:25,500 --> 00:26:27,460
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

613
00:26:27,544 --> 00:26:31,006
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

614
00:26:31,089 --> 00:26:32,841
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

615
00:26:32,924 --> 00:26:33,925
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
